      "writtenOn": "2016-10-27T19:02:01Z",
      "side": 0,
      "message": "Taking the path to PWBBTN_STATE_BOOT_KB_RESET will avoid shutdown caused by the CL:305037 but still maintain the purpose of that patch if the power button is release then press and hold again.\n\nI have tested this on a different platform, press and hold the power button from G3/S5 will power on the system, which is not what you wanted per the last update, but taking the path to PWRBTN_STATE_BOOT_KB_RESET will only assert the PCH_PWRBTN_L for 200ms, so the path from CL:305037 will not be executed and the system will not shutdown when the user release the power button.\n\nShawn/Randall, do you know the original reason for PWRBTN_STATE_WAS_OFF to keep PCH_PWRBTN_L asserted if press and hold from G3/S5?",
      "parentUuid": "46fd4226_1e2cedb0",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 295,
        "startChar": 18,
        "endLine": 295,
        "endChar": 38
      },
      "revId": "fa5afa458859f542c13840fd04d01696f4fa0231",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
